  "user_request_original": "Design a 36-layer periodic dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Stack structure: Air | (Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Gao)) repeated 18 times | Fused Silica. Initialize layer thicknesses near quarter-wave condition at 355 nm (Ta2O5 (Gao) approximately 62 nm, SiO2 (Gao) approximately 95 nm based on typical refractive indices). Optimize all 36 individual layer thicknesses within 20-350 nm bounds to minimize average transmittance in 355-365 nm and 1030-1080 nm bands while maximizing average transmittance in 420-700 nm band. Report final layer thickness sequence and transmittance spectra across 350-1100 nm.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design and optimize a 36-layer periodic dielectric filter consisting of 18 repetitions of Ta2O5/SiO2 on a fused silica substrate, with air incidence at 0 degrees under unpolarized light. Optimize all 36 layer thicknesses within 20–350 nm bounds to minimize average transmittance in 355–365 nm and 1030–1080 nm bands, and maximize average transmittance in 420–700 nm.",
